00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:39.400
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.600
Question 1 - Matthew Tam.

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.291
If Gallifrey was locked in the pocket universe
how did the TARDIS get there?

00:00:45.291 --> 00:00:48.060
There are two ways you can think about this.

00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:54.860
The first is that it wasn’t gallifrey and
the other is that Moffat never intends to

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.050
explicitly say yes or no this is or is not
Gallifrey.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:01:02.200
The reason I said it was Gallifrey in my review
video was because I read a spoiler from TV

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:07.170
Guide magazine that said Series 8 would include
a stop-over on gallifrey, but not a proper

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.299
Doctor visit.

00:01:08.299 --> 00:01:10.590
Obviously they were talking about this episode.

00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:14.119
TV Guide is generally known for being really
good with it’s facts so I didn’t doubt

00:01:14.119 --> 00:01:15.119
them.

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:18.600
Some of you have pointed out that the way
they cut the scene with the john hurt footage

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:22.990
causes some logic issues because Gallifrey
doesn’t have a blue sky.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:28.859
So if TV Guide was wrong and it’s not Gallifrey,
it’s probably Karn, just because I think

00:01:28.859 --> 00:01:32.440
the barn is meant to be the Doctor’s childhood
home as well as the barn from the 50th just

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:33.609
as a nice visual trilogy.

00:01:33.609 --> 00:01:43.509
He goes to Karn to become the war doctor,
goes back to end the universe and then recently,

00:01:43.509 --> 00:01:46.289
we found that was also where he grew up before
going to the academy.

00:01:46.289 --> 00:01:50.579
We’ll call that the “Not Gallifrey”
explanation.

00:01:50.579 --> 00:01:56.240
I think in Real Life, Moffat, when pressed
about this at conventions, will just use the

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:00.119
same type of logic he used to get them to
gallifrey in the 50th.

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:07.529
The Moment had timey wimey powers that were
able to negate the Time Lock.

00:02:07.529 --> 00:02:11.060
This episode wasn’t written till after the
50th Anniversary episode was written.

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:17.409
So when Moffat wrote the John Hurt Barn scene,
he didn’t know that he’d take them back

00:02:17.409 --> 00:02:18.670
there in series 8.

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:22.410
So I think a lot of the continuity issues
are just based on that.

00:02:22.410 --> 00:02:26.450
I still kind of think it’s Gallifrey and
Moffat tried to work within his own pre-established

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:28.459
canon and it got a little messy.

00:02:28.459 --> 00:02:30.370
Whatever the explanation really is, if it’s
something else.

00:02:30.370 --> 00:02:32.680
I don’t think it’s going to help the Doctor
bring Gallifrey back.

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:34.790
I think Gallifrey won’t come back anytime
soon.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:37.900
I think Missy and the finale will have something
to do with it.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:40.680
Not bringing it back, but finding it.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:47.610
Big takeaway, if you get really confused with
Moffat stories fitting into Canon, just think

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:48.610
like Moffat.

00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:51.049
And try to keep it simple.

00:02:51.049 --> 00:02:53.200
Question 2 - Septogram 7.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:58.159
Do you think The Doctor will ever show Clara
the Toy Soldier or realize she was the one

00:02:58.159 --> 00:03:00.349
who gave it to him?

00:03:00.349 --> 00:03:04.250
The Doctor stores all kinds of things from
each of his lives in the TARDIS, so it’s

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:11.489
possible the toy soldier is somewhere hidden
away and forgotten.

00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:16.920
But I think the soldier will be more important
as a metaphor for the finale.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:18.700
As it relates to Danny Pink and Missy.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:19.700
I don’t think the actual toy soldier itself
will be as important.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:23.810
I do like the idea that The First Doctor kept
it with him when he went to the academy and

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:26.849
then later when he stole the TARDIS.

00:03:26.849 --> 00:03:30.060
Question 3 - Dbz Axel.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.400
Any thoughts on Courtney the girl from Coal
Hill School?

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:36.599
She’s been mentioned or appeared in most
of the episodes so far?

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:38.620
I think there are two possible explanations.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:44.120
One is that they’re just trying to make
Coal Hill feel like more of a real place that

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:46.420
exists even when the Doctor and Clara aren’t
around.

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:48.689
So they just create characters that are associated
with it.

00:03:48.689 --> 00:03:52.750
And the other explanation is that yes she
is extra special and will have something to

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:54.460
do with a future episode.

00:03:54.460 --> 00:04:01.640
The synopsis for The Caretaker episode implies
that The Doctor will go to Coal Hill himself.

00:04:01.640 --> 00:04:06.750
That episode was written by Gareth Edwards,
who wrote The Lodger and Closing Time, two

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:10.299
episodes where the Doctor went and spent time
away from his companions.

00:04:10.299 --> 00:04:18.250
So the doctor could wind up spending a lot
of time with this courtney person in the episode.

00:04:18.250 --> 00:04:20.489
Question 4 - Dayvis.

00:04:20.489 --> 00:04:23.889
Is Danny Pink ever going to go on a proper
adventure with the Doctor or will he always

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:26.419
be stuck in present day?

00:04:26.419 --> 00:04:32.790
Samuel Anderson clarified his status a little
by saying he’s a companion to the companion.

00:04:32.790 --> 00:04:39.370
But I believe I read somewhere that he will
actually go on board the TARDIS at some point.

00:04:39.370 --> 00:04:41.920
I don’t know if that’s in the next couple
of weeks or if it’s only near the finale.

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:42.920
But I don’t think he’ll have an adventure
without Clara also being there.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:43.920
At least based on what Anderson is implying.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.330
There’s actually a funny story he told about
what he was doing when he found out he got

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.330
the show.

00:04:48.330 --> 00:04:51.210
He said his agent called and told he he’d
booked it.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:54.750
Then because he was in a room with a bunch
of his friends he told them and they all cheered.

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:57.509
But then his agent called back and said, don’t
tell anyone…

00:04:57.509 --> 00:05:11.199
And he was like, “I just told a room full
of people…”

00:05:11.199 --> 00:05:13.840
Question 5 - Programmer X.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:15.590
Was there something under the bed?

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:19.310
What was under the covers and what’s under
your bed?

00:05:19.310 --> 00:05:20.710
Yes there was definitely something under the
bed.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:23.530
You can interpret it as you want, but I think
they were meant to be a new monster that we’d

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:24.880
just never see full on.

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:29.220
As in, we’d never see what’s under the
bedsheet.

00:05:29.220 --> 00:05:32.509
As a story telling device, it’s great.

00:05:32.509 --> 00:05:38.520
Because Moffat doesn’t have to spend money
on special effects and makeup.

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.990
Capaldi’s doctor has been backtracking a
lot on some of his conclusions.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:45.099
So it’s totally possible the hands under
the bed belong to other people, not monsters.

00:05:45.099 --> 00:05:50.639
I think it’s another one of those Moffat
things, where he has the premise in his head

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:52.770
about the shared nightmare and he’s like,
what if we can never know what they look like.

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:56.210
And he just wants everyone to argue about
whether or not they a real deal new monster

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.010
or if there’s a more logical explanation.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:06:01.250
Question 6 - Dark Neko Studio.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:06.470
Why hasn’t the doctor been trying to find
gallifrey or repair his mistakes of the past?

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:09.460
That’s what I think the Blackboards are
all about.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:11.240
All the quantum physics equations.

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:15.870
He said when he wrote Listen, he wanted to
show what the Doctor does, when he’s all

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.840
by himself with nothing to do.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:22.229
So what I think is happening is, The Doctor
is taking his time in finding Gallifrey, it’s

00:06:22.229 --> 00:06:24.849
not going anywhere and the Time Lords are
safe, as far as we know.

00:06:24.849 --> 00:06:29.379
And I think this story was just a pause in
the fixing mistakes of the past.

00:06:29.379 --> 00:06:32.840
It’s hard to tell how urgent he was when
he said it was time to start correcting things.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:45.550
He wasn’t shouting it at Clara, so it seems
like he’s not in a rush.

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.640
Question 7 - Aliya Aliyaa.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:51.419
What if the boy under the blanket wasn’t
the Doctor but the Master?

00:06:51.419 --> 00:06:53.550
That’s a really interesting thought!

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.530
It would be a big WTF twist.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:57.884
But the reason I think it was the Doctor is
because of the way the Doctor explained all

00:06:57.884 --> 00:06:58.884
the Danny Pink run-ins.

00:06:58.884 --> 00:07:00.680
Clara was slaved to the TARDIS so it was traveling
to people connected to her timestream.

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:05.900
So for it to take her to The Master, she would
at some time have had to interact with him

00:07:05.900 --> 00:07:07.030
in a substantial way.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:10.650
There was gallifreyan clara, but I think that’s
reaching a bit far.

00:07:10.650 --> 00:07:15.449
There was someone in the comments that suggested
the Doctor was crying because it was around

00:07:15.449 --> 00:07:19.030
the time he and the Master were exposed to
the Untempered Schism.

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:21.800
The moment when the Doctor started to hear
the drum beats.

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:23.680
That’s totally possible too.

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:30.310
I don’t think that’s what Moffat was thinking
when he wrote the doctor crying in his sleep

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:31.310
though.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.870
Question 8 - The Elijah Talk.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.580
Can we mention it’s implied Clara and Danny
settle down?

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:41.090
It’s definitely implied, but when Orson
Pink said Time Travel runs in the family he

00:07:41.090 --> 00:07:46.650
could also have just been referencing Danny
Pink’s relationship with The Doctor and

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:47.650
Clara.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.440
Not that they ended up getting married and
having children.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:54.450
I don’t want to make too many Danny Clara
theories before seeing the finale.

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:58.550
Because supposedly there are crazy things
happening that would negate a lot of those

00:07:58.550 --> 00:07:59.669
theories.

00:07:59.669 --> 00:08:03.069
Companions totally get to settle down, but
I think it’s tradition for them to meet

00:08:03.069 --> 00:08:04.069
some untimely end.

00:08:04.069 --> 00:08:05.069
Like with Amy, Rory and the weeping Angels.

00:08:05.069 --> 00:08:09.980
They got to get married and have a child,
but they still became prisoners of the angels.

00:08:09.980 --> 00:08:14.150
Question 9 - Walking Who.

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:18.090
How do you feel about the Doctor not knowing
where they were during the barn scene?

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:20.230
Do you think he should know?

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:24.819
Assuming he doesn’t know about it, I think
it’s okay.

00:08:24.819 --> 00:08:28.780
The scene where clara told him to never go
back was more about him trusting her.

00:08:28.780 --> 00:08:33.000
And the idea of broken trust is a big deal
over the course of series 8.

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:35.810
The doctor trusting people and them breaking
that trust.

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:38.320
People trusting the doctor and him breaking
that trust.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:41.709
I think it will all play into whatever Missy
is doing.

00:08:41.709 --> 00:08:43.729
Question 10 - Rob Rubb.

00:08:43.729 --> 00:08:47.730
With both the episode and Doctor Who Extra
making deliberate references to the Doctor’s

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:52.000
past, will we see a moffat loop that takes
the story back to another major first doctor

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:53.480
moment like stealing the TARDIS?

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.790
I like that you call it a Moffat Loop, like
it’s a mobius strip or something.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:02.130
I do think that Missy will have something
to do with his ancient past, like back to

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:03.269
the first doctor.

00:09:03.269 --> 00:09:05.839
But I don’t think it will be related to
him stealing the TARDIS.

00:09:05.839 --> 00:09:09.589
I think it will be a big moment from the past
we haven’t ever seen before.

00:09:09.589 --> 00:09:13.540
Although there is a big scene in the finale
that’s a direct homage to a second doctor

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:14.540
scene.

00:09:14.540 --> 00:09:15.540
They did that scene in the series 7 finale
with gallifreyan clara telling him which TARDIS

00:09:15.540 --> 00:09:16.540
to steal.

00:09:16.540 --> 00:09:17.540
But I don’t think Moffat’s carrying that
forward.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:18.540
I’m starting to think Missy is someone totally
new, but new in that she’s never been done

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:19.540
before, but she’s someone from the Doctor’s
past.

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:20.540
I’m not expecting to see other versions
of the doctor on screen with Capaldi.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:21.540
Thanks so much for submitting questions, I
don’t think we’ll ever be completely satisfied

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:24.291
with the Barn theories but that’s just one
more big question to ask Moffat himself if

00:09:24.291 --> 00:09:26.459
you ever get the chance.

